import mundane theorem    stdlib/numbers/zero-product

theorem square-sum-zero
  note        (x + y)² is x² + 2xy + y², so it equals x² + y² exactly when
              2xy is 0, that is, when x or y is 0.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  let y ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  then (x + y)² = x² + y² ↔ x = 0 or y = 0

1.  (x + y)² = x² + y² ↔ x = 0 or y = 0
    both directions

    direction
    assume (x + y)² = x² + y²                                         (D1)

    1.1.  x·y = 0
          algebra, from D1

    1.2.  x = 0 or y = 0
          mun:zero-product, from 1.1

    direction
    assume x = 0 or y = 0                                             (D2)

    1.3.  (x + y)² = x² + y²
          cases, from D2

          case
          assume x = 0                                                (C1)

          1.3.1.  (x + y)² = x² + y²
                  algebra, from C1

          case
          assume y = 0                                                (C2)

          1.3.2.  (x + y)² = x² + y²
                  algebra, from C2
